NODE: crawler_schema | modules/crawler_schema | lang: rust | tier: 0 | deps: []
  READS: [seam-mappings/crawler-seam-mapping.md#1.3 Exhaustive transformation rule, seam-mappings/crawler-seam-mapping.md#3.1 Type notation, seam-mappings/crawler-seam-mapping.md#3.2 Missingness, seam-mappings/crawler-seam-mapping.md#4. Crawler Artifact Schemas]
  EXPOSES: [pub struct CheckedRecord { schema_id: String, value: serde_json::Value }, pub struct Fault { pub code: String, pub detail: String }, pub enum SourceEntity { Listing, ClassifierResult, WorkItem, JobDetail, CoverageLedger, CursorState, SessionState, AuditLog, StateMutationRecord, DeadLetter, SeenIds }, pub fn validate(schema_id: &str, value: serde_json::Value) -> Result<CheckedRecord, Fault>, pub fn record_value(record: &CheckedRecord) -> &serde_json::Value, pub fn record_schema(record: &CheckedRecord) -> &str]
  CONSUMES: []
  TEST_ASSERTIONS: [C02]
  INVARIANTS: [EK-NULL, EK-ASSESSMENT, EXT-TIME-NULL, OWD-OWNER]
  FORBIDDEN:
    - Accepting unknown versions, duplicate mapping keys, non-finite numbers, undeclared closed-object fields, or normalized null outside Missing.value.
    - Treating schema validation as authorization, digest verification, capability certification, or satisfaction of cross-record semantic rules.
    - Inserting default success, zero, false, empty collections, fabricated content, or a seventh NullReason.
    - Adding fields to closed shared contracts or collapsing capability, opportunity, and result.
  VERIFICATION: cargo test -p crawler_schema -- c02

